statement:
Let $G$ be a finite two-player zero-sum game with $M \ge 1$ row actions and $N$ column actions, given by a payoff matrix $A$ with $0 \le A_{ij} \le 1$, and fix a pure column action $j$. Let $T > 0$ and let $p_0, \dots, p_{T-1}$ be probability distributions over the $M$ row actions, each presented as non-negative weights $p_t(i)$ summing to $1$, and let $\bar{p}$ be their average strategy, the mixed row strategy with weights $\bar{p}_i = \frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1} p_t(i)$. Then the expected payoff of $\bar{p}$ against column $j$ satisfies
\[
  \sum_{i} \bar{p}_i \, A_{ij}
  \;=\;
  \frac{1}{T} \sum_{t=0}^{T-1} \sum_{i} p_t(i) \, A_{ij}.
\]
